IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Carriage by Air Act 1988 (2020 Revised Edition), Singapore Statutes Online, current
-- version as at 30 Sep 2026.  Source: source/CAA1988.txt (extracted from source/CAA1988.pdf).
--
-- The shared nouns, and nothing else: DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Every other module imports this one.
--
-- The Act (ss 1 to 13) gives the force of law in Singapore to three texts of the Warsaw
-- Convention, set out in the three Schedules.  They are three versions of one convention and
-- differ in limits, time limits, documents and defences.  Each is its own answer: the
-- version is an input (`Convention`) to every rule where the versions differ, and a version
-- that says nothing on a point answers with silence (REFUSE), never with a figure taken from
-- another version.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does
-- answering it require reading the Act or the Convention?  Only the first kind is a field.
-- Whether a State is a "High Contracting Party" for a given territory, whether a foreign law
-- treats a default as equivalent to wilful misconduct, and what an SDR is worth on the day of
-- judgment are answers from outside the Act and are fields, not rules.

§ `The three texts`

DECLARE Convention IS ONE OF
    `the Warsaw Convention`
    `the Warsaw (Hague) Convention`
    `the Warsaw (Hague) (Montreal) Convention`

DECLARE `Kind of Thing Carried` IS ONE OF
    `a passenger`
    `registered baggage`
    `cargo`

DECLARE `Ground of Liability` IS ONE OF
    `the death or wounding of a passenger or other bodily injury to a passenger`
    `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage`
    `the destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo`
    `delay in the carriage by air of passengers, baggage or cargo`

DECLARE `Kind of Limit` IS ONE OF
    `the liability for each passenger in the carriage of persons`
    `the liability for registered baggage`
    `the liability for cargo`
    `the liability for objects of which the passenger takes charge himself`

DECLARE Unit IS ONE OF
    Francs
    `Special Drawing Rights`

DECLARE `Liability Limit` HAS
    `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the unit` IS A Unit
    `the amount is per kilogramme` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The Act: nouns of sections 2 to 13`

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 2 'court'"
DECLARE `Arbitration Facts` HAS
    `the proceedings are an arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arbitration is allowed by a Convention` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 3(1)"
DECLARE `Force of Law Facts` HAS
    `the provisions relate to the rights and liabilities of carriers, carriers' employees and agents, passengers, consignors, consignees or other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is carriage by air to which the Convention applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nationality of the aircraft performing the carriage` IS A STRING

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 4(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `State Facts` HAS
    `the State has ratified or acceded to the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State is a party to the Convention in respect of the territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State has availed itself of the provisions of the Additional Protocol` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(1) to (3)"
DECLARE `Limited Proceedings Facts` HAS
    `the proceedings enforce a liability limited by Article 22` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the liability is or may be partly enforceable in other proceedings in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amounts awarded or recoverable in those other proceedings` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 6(4)"
DECLARE `Equivalent Facts` HAS
    `the Minister has by order specified an equivalent in Singapore dollars for one unit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the equivalent in Singapore dollars of one unit specified by the order` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 7 and Article 26(2)"
DECLARE `Partial Loss Facts` HAS
    `part of the baggage or cargo is lost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the remainder was received` IS A DATE
    `the date the whole was received` IS A DATE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8, and Article 29"
DECLARE `Carriage End` IS ONE OF
    `the aircraft arrived at the destination` HAS
        `the date of arrival at the destination` IS A DATE
    `the aircraft did not arrive` HAS
        `the date the aircraft ought to have arrived` IS A DATE
    `the carriage stopped` HAS
        `the date the carriage stopped` IS A DATE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8(1) and (4)"
DECLARE `Employee Action Facts` HAS
    `the action arises out of damage to which a Convention relates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is against the carrier's employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee or agent was acting within the scope of his or her employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the carriage ended` IS A `Carriage End`
    `the date the action or arbitration is brought` IS A DATE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 8(3) and (4)"
DECLARE `Contribution Facts` HAS
    `the person seeks to recover contribution in respect of damage to which a Convention relates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the court gave judgment or made an award against the person seeking contribution` IS A DATE
    `the date the action or arbitration for contribution is brought` IS A DATE
    `the last day allowed by sections 4 and 29 of the Limitation Act 1959, where they extend the time` IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 10"
DECLARE `Military Facts` HAS
    `the Minister has by order directed that section 10 applies to the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is of persons, cargo or baggage for the military authorities of that State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aircraft is registered in that State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the whole capacity of the aircraft has been reserved by or on behalf of those authorities` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Carriage by Air Act 1988, s 11"
DECLARE `Party Action Facts` HAS
    `the State is a High Contracting Party to a Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State has availed itself of the provisions of the Additional Protocol` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is brought in a court in Singapore in accordance with Article 28` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is in respect of carriage undertaken by the High Contracting Party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an enforcement order is sought against the property of the High Contracting Party` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The Convention: nouns of Chapter I, scope`

@ref "Convention, Article 1(1) and (2), Article 2, Article 34, Additional Protocol"
DECLARE `Carriage Facts` HAS
    `the carriage is of persons, baggage or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is performed by aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is gratuitous carriage performed by an air transport undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `according to the agreement between the parties the places of departure and destination are within the territories of two High Contracting Parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State or Power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is performed by the State or by a legally constituted public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is performed directly by the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State has availed itself of the Additional Protocol as to Article 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is of mail and postal packages, or is performed under the terms of an international postal Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is performed by way of experimental trial by air navigation undertakings with a view to the establishment of a regular line of air navigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is performed in extraordinary circumstances outside the normal scope of an air carrier's business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 1(3)"
DECLARE `Successive Carriage Facts` HAS
    `the carriage is to be performed by several successive air carriers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties have regarded it as a single operation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one contract or a series of contracts is to be performed entirely within the territory of the same State` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The Convention: nouns of Chapter II, documents of carriage`

DECLARE Forfeiture IS ONE OF
    `nothing is forfeited`
    `Article 22 is forfeited`
    `Article 22(2) is forfeited`
    `every provision of the Convention that excludes or limits the carrier's liability is forfeited`

@ref "Convention, Article 3"
DECLARE `Ticket Facts` HAS
    `a passenger ticket was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket states the place and date of issue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket states the places of departure and destination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket states the agreed stopping places` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket states the name and address of the carrier or carriers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket indicates at least one such stopping place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ticket contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for death or personal injury and for loss of or damage to baggage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier accepted the passenger, or with the carrier's consent the passenger embarked, without a passenger ticket having been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 4"
DECLARE `Baggage Check Facts` HAS
    `the baggage is other than small personal objects of which the passenger takes charge himself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a baggage check was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the baggage check is made out in duplicate, one part for the passenger and one for the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the place and date of issue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the places of departure and destination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the name and address of the carrier or carriers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the number of the passenger ticket` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states that delivery of the baggage will be made to the bearer of the check` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the number and weight of the packages` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states the amount of the value declared` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the baggage check is combined with or incorporated in a passenger ticket that complies with Article 3` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check indicates at least one such stopping place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the check contains the notice that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to baggage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier took charge of the baggage without a baggage check having been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Articles 5 to 9"
DECLARE `Waybill Facts` HAS
    `an air waybill was made out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the air waybill was made out in three original parts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first part is marked "for the carrier" and signed by the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second part is marked "for the consignee" and signed by the consignor and the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the third part is signed by the carrier and handed to the consignor after the cargo has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier signed on acceptance of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier signed before the cargo was loaded on board the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the place and date of its execution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the places of departure and destination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the agreed stopping places` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the name and address of the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the name and address of the first carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the name and address of the consignee, if the case so requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the nature of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the number of the packages, the method of packing and the particular marks or numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the weight, the quantity and the volume or dimensions of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the apparent condition of the cargo and of the packing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the freight if agreed, the date and place of payment and who is to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states, if the cargo is sent for payment on delivery, the price and any expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the amount of the value declared` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the number of parts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the documents handed to the carrier to accompany it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states the time fixed for completion and a brief note of the route, if agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill states that the carriage is subject to the rules relating to liability established by the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the places of departure and destination are within the territory of a single High Contracting Party with an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill indicates at least one such stopping place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill contains the notice to the consignor that the Warsaw Convention may be applicable and governs and in most cases limits the liability of carriers for loss of or damage to cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the waybill or the receipt indicates the weight of the consignment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another means that preserves a record of the carriage was substituted, with the consignor's consent, for an air waybill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier accepted the cargo, or with the carrier's consent it was loaded on board the aircraft, without an air waybill having been made out` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Statement` IS ONE OF
    `a statement of the weight, dimensions or packing of the cargo, or the number of packages`
    `a statement of the quantity, volume or condition of the cargo`

@ref "Convention, Article 11(2)"
DECLARE `Statement Facts` HAS
    `kind of statement` IS A `Kind of Statement`
    `the statement was checked by the carrier in the presence of the consignor and is stated in the waybill to have been` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement relates to the apparent condition of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 10"
DECLARE `Indemnity Facts` HAS
    `the damage is suffered by the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is suffered by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier is liable to that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the particulars and statements furnished by the consignor or on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the particulars and statements inserted by the carrier or on his behalf in the receipt or record` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is suffered by the consignor or by a person to whom the consignor is liable` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Articles 12 to 14"
DECLARE `Disposition Facts` HAS
    `the consignee's right under Article 13 has begun` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consignee declines to accept the air waybill or the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consignee cannot be communicated with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier obeyed the consignor's orders without requiring production of the part of the air waybill or the receipt delivered to the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damage has been caused to a person lawfully in possession of that part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is impossible to carry out the orders of the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier has informed the consignor forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 13(3)"
DECLARE `Delivery Facts` HAS
    `the carrier admits the loss of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cargo has arrived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the cargo ought to have arrived` IS A DATE
    `the date on which the rights are asserted` IS A DATE

@ref "Convention, Article 16"
DECLARE `Customs Facts` HAS
    `the consignor furnished the information and documents necessary to meet the formalities of customs, octroi or police` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier has suffered damage occasioned by their absence, insufficiency or irregularity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is due to the fault of the carrier or his servants or agents` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The Convention: nouns of Chapter III, liability`

@ref "Convention, Article 17"
DECLARE `Passenger Accident Facts` HAS
    `the damage is death, wounding or other bodily injury suffered by a passenger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident which caused the damage took place on board the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident took place in the course of any of the operations of embarking or disembarking` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 18"
DECLARE `Cargo Loss Facts` HAS
    `the damage is destruction or loss of, or damage to, registered baggage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is destruction or loss of, or damage to, cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occurrence which caused the damage took place during the carriage by air` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the baggage or cargo was in the charge of the carrier in an aerodrome or airport, on board an aircraft, or in any place after a landing outside an aerodrome` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occurrence took place in carriage by land, sea or river performed outside an aerodrome or airport` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that carriage took place in the performance of a contract for carriage by air, for the purpose of loading, delivery or transhipment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is proof to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that the loss or damage resulted solely from an inherent defect, quality or vice of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from defective packaging of the cargo by a person other than the carrier or his servants or agents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from an act of war or an armed conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that it resulted solely from an act of public authority carried out in connexion with the entry, exit or transit of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 20"
DECLARE `Defence Facts` HAS
    `the carrier proves that he and his servants and agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that it was impossible for him and them to take such measures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that the damage was occasioned by negligent pilotage or negligence in the handling of the aircraft or in navigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that in all other respects he and his agents have taken all necessary measures to avoid the damage` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 21"
DECLARE `Contributory Negligence Facts` HAS
    `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence of the person suffering the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier proves that the damage was caused by or contributed to by the negligence or other wrongful act or omission of the person claiming compensation or the person from whom he derives his rights` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 22(1) to (3)"
DECLARE `Limit Facts` HAS
    `the passenger and the carrier have agreed by special contract a higher limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the higher limit agreed` IS A NUMBER
    `a special declaration of interest in delivery at destination was made at the time the package was handed over and any supplementary sum has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the declared sum` IS A NUMBER
    `the carrier proves that the declared sum is greater than the actual interest in delivery at destination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the actual interest in delivery at destination` IS A NUMBER
    `the total weight in kilogrammes of the package or packages concerned` IS A NUMBER
    `the loss, damage or delay of part affects the value of other packages covered by the same baggage check or air waybill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total weight in kilogrammes of those other packages` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Convention, Article 22(4)"
DECLARE `Costs Facts` HAS
    `the amount of the damages awarded, excluding court costs and other expenses of the litigation` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum the carrier offered in writing to the plaintiff, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the date of the occurrence causing the damage` IS A DATE
    `the date the action was commenced` IS A DATE
    `the date the carrier made the offer, if it was made` IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref "Convention, Articles 25 and 25A"
DECLARE `Limit Breaking Facts` HAS
    `the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier done with intent to cause damage or recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage resulted from such an act or omission of a servant or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the servant or agent was acting within the scope of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is caused by the wilful misconduct of the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is caused by such default of the carrier as, according to the law of the court seised of the case, is considered equivalent to wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damage is so caused by a servant or agent of the carrier acting within the scope of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 25A(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Servant Limit Facts` HAS
    `an action is brought against a servant or agent of the carrier arising out of damage to which the Convention relates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the servant or agent proves that he acted within the scope of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount recoverable from the carrier` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount recoverable from his servants and agents` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Kind of Complaint` IS ONE OF
    `damage to baggage`
    `damage to cargo`
    `delay of baggage`
    `delay of cargo`

@ref "Convention, Article 26"
DECLARE `Complaint Facts` HAS
    `kind of complaint` IS A `Kind of Complaint`
    `the date of receipt, or the date the baggage or cargo was placed at the disposal of the person entitled to delivery` IS A DATE
    `the date the damage was discovered` IS A DATE
    `the date the complaint was made` IS A DATE
    `the complaint was made forthwith after the discovery of the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complaint is in writing upon the document of carriage or by separate notice in writing despatched within the times` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier was guilty of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 28"
DECLARE `Jurisdiction Facts` HAS
    `the court is in the territory of one of the High Contracting Parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier is ordinarily resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier has his principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has jurisdiction where the carrier has an establishment by which the contract has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has jurisdiction at the place of destination` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 29"
DECLARE `Limitation Facts` HAS
    `how the carriage ended` IS A `Carriage End`
    `the date the action is brought` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Claimant` IS ONE OF
    `the passenger or the passenger's representative`
    `the consignor`
    `the consignee who is entitled to delivery`

DECLARE `Position of the Carrier` IS ONE OF
    `the first carrier`
    `the last carrier`
    `the carrier who performed the carriage during which the accident or the delay occurred`
    `the carrier who performed the carriage during which the destruction, loss, damage or delay took place`
    `another carrier`

@ref "Convention, Article 30"
DECLARE `Successive Action Facts` HAS
    `the carriage is to be performed by various successive carriers and falls within Article 1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carrier accepted passengers, baggage or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant` IS A Claimant
    `the claim concerns` IS A `Kind of Thing Carried`
    `position` IS A `Position of the Carrier`
    `by express agreement the first carrier has assumed liability for the whole journey` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The Convention: nouns of Chapters IV and V`

@ref "Convention, Articles 23 and 32"
DECLARE `Clause Facts` HAS
    `the clause tends to relieve the carrier of liability or to fix a lower limit than that laid down in the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the clause is a provision governing loss or damage resulting from the inherent defect, quality or vice of the cargo carried` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the clause or special agreement purports to infringe the rules of the Convention, whether by deciding the law to be applied or by altering the rules as to jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the clause or agreement was entered into before the damage occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the clause is an arbitration clause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage is of cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arbitration is to take place within one of the jurisdictions referred to in the first paragraph of Article 28` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Article 31"
DECLARE `Combined Carriage Facts` HAS
    `the carriage is performed partly by air and partly by another mode of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carriage by air falls within the terms of Article 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties inserted in the document of air carriage conditions relating to another mode of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provisions of the Convention are observed as regards the carriage by air` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Convention, Articles 37 to 39 and 40A"
DECLARE `Treaty Facts` HAS
    `the date the fifth instrument of ratification was deposited` IS A DATE
    `the date the instrument of ratification of the State is deposited` IS A DATE
    `the date the notification of accession is made` IS A DATE
    `the date the notification of denunciation is made` IS A DATE
    `the number of instruments of ratification deposited by that date` IS A NUMBER
    `the State's ratification or adherence has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State's denunciation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Regulative duties: the parties and acts`

DECLARE `Party to the Convention` IS ONE OF
    `The carrier`
    `The consignor`

DECLARE `Act under the Convention` IS ONE OF
    `give notice to the consignee of the arrival of the cargo`
    `inform the consignor of the impossibility of carrying out his orders`
    `complain to the carrier in writing about damage or delay`
